;;; A written `eq` fact is stored, not checked against its definition — M1f
;;; **W50**, register row `W50/fact-eq-false` (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`),
;;; filed by S1f.5.7 (T1f.5.7.1, 2026-11-09) from its step 1's probes, `open`
;;; and owned by S1f.5.7, on the user's ruling of 2026-11-07 (Q-M1e2.26: `eq`
;;; and `neq` are relations whose facts are fixed by name identity, computed
;;; and never stored, and no fact, rule or commitment changes them) and its
;;; G-21 (a rule may conclude a false one, which is a contradiction).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; One fact `(p a)` and the written fact `(eq a w)`.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; A fact is a conclusion with no premise, so a written fact of `eq` is
;;; checked as a rule's conclusion of one is (G-21; Q-M1f.33, taken by default
;;; on the user's instruction of 2026-11-09): `a` and `w` are two names, so
